{%- comment -%}
  Russian second-level product bar (DDS-Foundations redesign, Figma variant Type=Second level).
  The English bar stays in _includes/header-l2-menu.liquid and is untouched.
  The product lookup below is copied from it verbatim; only the markup around it is new.

  #bottom-header-nav, .nav__trigger, .menu-item-has-children--bottom and the
  ".header.header__product-menu ul.nav li" selector used by the inline scripts in the
  layouts are all preserved.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign productCode = page.product_code | default: "deckhouse-platform" %}
{%- if productCode == "kubernetes-platform" %}{% assign productCode = "deckhouse-platform" %}{% endif %}
{%- if productCode == "development-platform" %}{% assign productCode = "development-portal" %}{% endif %}
{%- assign _conditionProductURL = "/products/" | append: productCode | append: "/" %}
{%- assign productMenuData = l2MenuData | where: "url", _conditionProductURL | first %}
{%- assign productMenuDataFallback = l2MenuDataFallback | where: "url", _conditionProductURL | first %}
{%- assign productLogoURL = "/images/sprite.svg?v2#" | append: productCode | append: "-icon" %}
{%- assign productName = productMenuData.title %}
{%- unless productMenuData %}
  {%- assign productName = productMenuDataFallback.title %}
{%- endunless %}
{%- comment -%}
  Brand lockups, taken from the live site. Every product ships one on a uniform 120x36
  canvas - that is what keeps this bar the same height on every product page, since the
  row is as tall as its tallest child. Development Platform is the one exception at
  120x37, and the live site's bar is 63px on that page for exactly the same reason, so
  the odd pixel is reproduced rather than squashed.
  Anything not listed keeps the previous mark + title, so an uncovered product still
  renders correctly.
  zoom-image-disable on the lockup below: assets/js/zoom-image.js makes every <img>
  inside .content a GLightbox target and sets an inline cursor: zoom-in on it, and the
  header renders inside that wrapper. The class is that script's own opt-out (:339).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign productLockup = "" %}
{%- assign lockupW = "120" %}
{%- assign lockupH = "36" %}
{%- case productCode %}
  {%- when "deckhouse-platform" %}{% assign productLockup = "platform" %}
  {%- when "stronghold" %}{% assign productLockup = "stronghold" %}
  {%- when "observability-platform" %}{% assign productLockup = "observability" %}
  {%- when "code" %}{% assign productLockup = "code" %}
  {%- when "development-platform" %}{% assign productLockup = "development-platform" %}{% assign lockupH = "37" %}
  {%- when "development-portal" %}{% assign productLockup = "development-platform" %}{% assign lockupH = "37" %}
{%- endcase %}
{%- comment -%}
  Solutions live in the Deckhouse Platform bar, as on deckhouse.ru. The API sends them as a
  bare link to /solutions/; the site opens it as a two-column panel of solutions with
  descriptions, which the feed does not carry, so the list is hardcoded here and the
  item's own title and URL still come from the API.
  A feed without that item - the copy of the data committed to the repo, which local
  builds use - gets it inserted after Extensions, so the menu does not silently lose it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign solutionsInFeed = productMenuData.items | where: "url", "/solutions/" | size %}
{%- assign solutionsInFeedNoSlash = productMenuData.items | where: "url", "/solutions" | size %}
{%- assign solutionsInFeed = solutionsInFeed | plus: solutionsInFeedNoSlash %}
{%- capture solutionsPanel %}
    <div class="sub-menu-container">
      <ul class="sub-menu sub-menu_solutions">
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/containers">
            <span>Для контейнеров</span>
            <p>Микросервисные приложения на&nbsp;любой инфраструктуре</p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/virtualization">
            <span>Для виртуализации</span>
            <p>Виртуальные машины на&nbsp;современной платформе виртуализации</p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/mixed-workloads">
            <span>Для комбинированных нагрузок</span>
            <p>Контейнеры и&nbsp;виртуальные машины под&nbsp;единым управлением</p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/ai">
            <span>Для искусственного интеллекта</span>
            <p>Запуск ИИ&#8288;-&#8288;нагрузок в&nbsp;своей инфраструктуре</p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/data-orchestration">
            <span>Для данных</span>
            <p>Построение платформ хранения и&nbsp;обработки данных</p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/private-cloud">
            <span>Для частного облака</span>
            <p>Частное облако с&nbsp;биллингом и&nbsp;управляемыми сервисами</p>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="/solutions/hybrid-infrastructure">
            <span>Для гибридной инфраструктуры</span>
            <p>Приложения в&nbsp;любых средах под&nbsp;управлением из&nbsp;единой точки</p>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
{%- endcapture %}
<div class="header header__product-menu header__product-menu--ru">
  <div class="header__product-menu-inner container">
    <div class="header__product-menu-logo">
      {%- if productLockup != "" %}
        <img class="header__product-lockup zoom-image-disable" src="/images/header/logo-{{ productLockup }}.svg" width="{{ lockupW }}" height="{{ lockupH }}" alt="{{ productName }}">
      {%- else %}
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none">
          <use xlink:href="{{ productLogoURL }}"></use>
        </svg>
        <span>{{ productName }}</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="nav__trigger"></div>
    <ul id="bottom-header-nav" class="nav header__nav header__nav--bottom">
      {%- if productMenuData.items %}
        {%- for item in productMenuData.items %}
          {%- if item.url == "/solutions/" or item.url == "/solutions" %}{% assign isSolutions = true %}{% else %}{% assign isSolutions = false %}{% endif %}
          {%- if item.rel == "doc" %}{% assign itemClass='class="header__navigation-item active"' %}{% elsif isSolutions %}{% assign itemClass='class="header__navigation-item header__navigation-item--solutions menu-item-has-children menu-item-has-children--bottom"' %}{% elsif item.items %}{% assign itemClass='class="header__navigation-item menu-item-has-children menu-item-has-children--bottom"' %}{%- else %}{% assign itemClass='class="header__navigation-item"' %}{% endif %}
          <li {{ itemClass }} {%- if item.items or isSolutions %} data-proofer-ignore{% endif %}>
            <a href="{{ item.url }}"{% if item.target.size > 0 %} target="{{ item.target }}"{% endif %}>{{ item.title }}</a>
            {% if isSolutions %}
              {{ solutionsPanel }}
            {% elsif item.items %}
              <div class="sub-menu-container">
                <ul class="sub-menu">
                  {% for item in item.items %}
                    <li data-proofer-ignore><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.title }}</a></li>
                  {% endfor %}
                </ul>
              </div>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
          {%- if solutionsInFeed == 0 and productCode == "deckhouse-platform" and item.url == "/products/deckhouse-platform/extensions/" %}
          <li class="header__navigation-item header__navigation-item--solutions menu-item-has-children menu-item-has-children--bottom" data-proofer-ignore>
            <a href="/solutions/">Решения</a>
            {{ solutionsPanel }}
          </li>
          {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      {%- else %}
        <li class="header__navigation-item active" data-proofer-ignore>
          <a href="#">{{ site.data.i18n.common['documentation'][page.lang] | capitalize }}</a>
        </li>
      {%- endif %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
